;; Japan's purpose classification (目的別分類) of general-account expenditure
;; mapped to UN COFOG divisions, for awai-public-funds (AWAI-3294,
;; network-awai-apex ADR 0046 D3/D5).
;;
;; Every mapping here is :assumed: it is this profile's judgement, not a
;; statement by the Ministry of Finance or the UN. The code names come from
;; the 目的別分類 table in 「令和6年度 一般会計 当初予算」 (予算書・決算書データベース,
;; https://www.bb.mof.go.jp/server/2024/dlpdf/DL202411001.pdf, pp. 1136-1137,
;; sha256 d5031c98e8a1296985b5a12b3896ce7abc181e438ba57cca1b0639b9725a1883).
;; That table says the classification exists to help compute government
;; spending in the national accounts (国民経済計算), which is why it is used
;; as the bridge to COFOG.
;;
;; :confidence :high  the code's whole scope falls in one COFOG division.
;; :confidence :low   most of it does, but part belongs elsewhere (see :note).
;; :division nil      the code spans several divisions or is a reserve; its
;;                    amounts are reported as unmapped rather than guessed.
;; A code missing from this map is reported as unknown.
{:map/version "2026-11-18"
 :map/basis :assumed
 :cofog/divisions {"01" "General public services" "02" "Defence" "03" "Public order and safety"
                   "04" "Economic affairs" "05" "Environmental protection"
                   "06" "Housing and community amenities" "07" "Health"
                   "08" "Recreation, culture and religion" "09" "Education" "10" "Social protection"}
